# SAMPLE -- OVERLAY layer (ADR-0036), deliberately EMPTY.
#
# An existing empty directory is a CLAIM: "this deployment names no systems of record." That
# is a different statement from an UNSET overlay variable, which means "nobody told me where to
# look" and leaves the composed set unknowable -- same distinction `policy/overlays/sample/
# graphs/.gitkeep` draws for GRAPH_OVERLAY_DIRS, repeated here for
# SYSTEMS_OF_RECORD_OVERLAY_DIRS.
#
# Per the module docstring's quoted algorithm ("extracted identity -> first matching system's
# pattern -> connector lookup -> origin from the record. Miss or no pattern -> origin
# unresolved"), an empty composed set means every artifact's origin resolves to a miss here --
# which is today's sandbox behaviour, unchanged: an artifact with no recorded origin stays
# visible to its dropper/owner only. The seal path is proven instead by a TEST-ONLY
# system-of-record row pointing at `origin_resolver.CONNECTORS["sandbox-fake"]`, built in the
# test itself, never shipped here.
